<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">The Compact of Etheria</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;To give some background, this was originally posted on Google Docs for my "&lt;a href="https://archiveofourown.org/series/1514015" rel="nofollow"&gt;An Unlikely Alliance Against Evildoers&lt;/a&gt;" series. It was first mentioned in the first chapter of the fic "&lt;a href="https://archiveofourown.org/works/21583765" rel="nofollow"&gt;The Trial of Catra, Pearl's Ferocity, and 'Wild Adora'&lt;/a&gt;". This document has a key role in Entrapta sliding out of her punishment, as a mysterious Ms. Ehre in Mystacor lays out in the fourth chapter (entitled &lt;a href="https://archiveofourown.org/works/21673210/chapters/161012554" rel="nofollow"&gt;"Friends You Can Stand By: Perfuma's Present, Ms. Ehre's Offer, and Entrapta's New Role&lt;/a&gt;") of "From Deception to Devotion: The Diamonds, Adora, Perfuma, and Challenges in Japan," &lt;em&gt;basically&lt;/em&gt; creating a legal loophole for her! It again appears in parts 19 (chapter 4), 21, 23 (implied), and 24 (chapter 3) of that series.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I posted this doc. over a few days &lt;a href="https://squidgeworld.org/works/70418/chapters/141197" rel="nofollow"&gt;on Squidge World&lt;/a&gt; in early January of this year. Considering that I don't have any planned fanfics on this account for this year, as of yet, I decided to post this here.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>lefemmerouge</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
